{"id": "142161", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=142161", "title": "Johnson Creek", "text": "Johnson Creek is a small village in Jefferson County, Wisconsin.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nI-94 goes through Johnson Creek. State route WI-26 also runs through the city. It is 45 minutes from Madison on I-94 from the west, and 45 minutes from Milwaukee and 2 hr 15 min from Chicago on I-94 from the east. It is 2 hours from Green Bay on I-41 and WI-26."}
{"id": "142179", "revid": "2183461", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=142179", "title": "Champhai", "text": "Champhai is in Mizoram, Northeast India.\nUnderstand.\nChamphai is a local commercial hub on the Indo-Myanmar border, about 200 km from Aizawl, and has the biggest stretch of plains used for rice cultivation in Mizoram.\nGet in.\nThe only way to get into Champhai is by road. \nSumos (10 passenger SUV) are available to/from Aizawl (\u20b9450) and Lunglei (\u20b9750, 12 hr).\nBooking counters in Aizawl are around Lower Zarkawt (Electric Veng). The road to Champhai is narrow and winding, one should expect 8 hours journey including one meal stop on the way. Sumos leave both Champhai and Aizawl around 6AM and 6PM.\nNo Sumo runs on Sundays and Christian holidays.\nBuy.\nAs a commercial hub for Indo-Myanmar trade, there are many Myanmar products available in the market. Cheap staffs are more Chinese origin come through Myanmar rather than from main parts of India.\nMizos are devout Christians, and all stores and restaurants close their doors on Sundays and after 6PM.\nConnect.\nAirtel has by far the best 3G coverage in the area followed by Aircel. Vodafone, idea, Reliance have 2G coverage in the town area."}
